+- Independent policy126, actual Runtime104, encounter369 and concrete projectile38 checks passed on the first corrected753-input candidate. The runtime proof separates28 real configured damage-path observations from eight explicit late kill/pickup fault-injection controls. Current production kill/pickup effects do not naturally perform that injected immediate enemy damage; no new production proc was added.
+- A later independent8-check death-disposal probe found two real C3 cleanup failures: normal late projectile death removed the source before final support settlement, leaving channel fields in a retained dictionary. The target was not healed and no resurrection or memory leak was established. A new candidate adds only a support disposal call before the original death branch callbacks/removal. Original failed753 remains immutable. A distinct true-cold plus five-script regression passed8/126/104/369/38 with the original assertions and strict180-second limits.
+- Two old-encounter controls on the earlier candidate preserved the actual held v37 six-transaction and24-combat traces byte-for-byte. They do not substitute for the new candidate's required complete aggregate.
